  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASEAN Country Participants Assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Two small grants to the ASEAN Studies Center (ASC) at American University to provide assistance to ASEAN country participants, particularly subject matter experts from civil society, to build skills for participation in regional discussions in their areas of expertise. Topics of these discussions may include: ASEAN integration; steps needed to achieve an ASEAN Economic Community by 2015; transnational crime; water management; climate change; human rights and economic development. In prior years, participants from ASEAN countries have presented their analysis, gained exposure to U.S. and international technical experts, and developed sets of recommendations for ASEAN and U.S. Leaders. These trainings will build capacity of ASEAN Member nation participants in civil society and governance.hese events clarify issues of priority concern to ASEAN countries and the United States, while giving ASEAN experts the opportunity to engage with leading U.S. experts.</narrative>
  </description>
